  "articleBody": "Installing new bathroom fixtures can seem straightforward, but there are a few common pitfalls that can turn a simple upgrade into a major headache. First off, a big no-no is reusing old, corroded supply lines. They might look okay on the outside, but they're often ready to fail, leading to leaks down the road. Always replace them with new ones! Secondly, overtightening fittings is a classic mistake. You'd think tighter is better, but it can actually damage the pipes or the fixture itself. A gentle snug is usually all you need. Thirdly, never skip the leak test. After installation, turn on the water and carefully check all connections. A tiny drip can become a big problem quickly. Fourth, failing to clean the mounting surface properly can lead to an unstable or wobbly fixture. Take the time to make sure everything is spotless. And finally, one of the biggest blunders is finding out too late that your new fixture’s dimensions don’t match your existing space. Measure twice, buy once, as they say! If you're feeling overwhelmed or just want the job done right, consider calling in the experts at HH Remodeling LLC. We handle these details every day, so you don't have to.",
